 "infoPop": "The chance that rain or snow (usually 0.1–1 mm or more) falls during that hour, or during that day for daily forecasts.\n\n70% means that in similar situations it rained about 7 times out of 10. It is not how much rain falls or how many hours it rains.\n\nA range like 1–72% means sources disagree: the lowest says 1%, the highest 72%. Some sources give only amounts (mm), not a chance.\n\nBars: the light band is all sources' low to high; the dark bar is the middle low to middle high.",
